{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JHN",
  "chapter": 19,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Pilate therefore took Jesus, and scourged ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the soldiers platted a crown of thorns, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on his head, and they put on him a purple robe,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, Hail, King of the Jews! and they smote him with their hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pilate therefore went forth again, and saith to them, Behold, I bring him forth to you, that ye may know that I find no fault in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jesus came forth, wearing the crown of thorns, and the purple robe. And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pilate",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " saith to them, Behold the man!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When therefore the chief priests and officers saw him, they cried out, saying, Crucify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", crucify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Pilate saith to them, Take ye him, and crucify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": for I find no fault in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Jews answered him, We have a law, and by our law he ought to die, because he made himself the Son of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he was the more afraid;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And went again into the judgment-hall, and saith to Jesus, Whence art thou? But Jesus gave him no answer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith Pilate to him, Speakest thou not to me? knowest thou not, that I have power to crucify thee, and have power to release thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered, Thou couldst have no power against me; except it were given thee from above: therefore he that delivered me to thee hath the greater sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from thenceforth Pilate sought to release him: but the Jews cried out, saying, If thou let this man go, thou art not Cesar's friend. Whoever maketh himself a king, speaketh against Cesar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he brought Jesus forth, and sat down on the judgment-seat, in a place that is called the Pavement, but in the Hebrew, Gabbatha.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was the preparation of the passover, and about the sixth hour: and he saith to the Jews, Behold your King!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they cried out, Away with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", away with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", crucify him. Pilate saith to them, Shall I crucify your King? The chief priests answered, We have no king but Cesar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then therefore he delivered him to them to be crucified. And they took Jesus, and led ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he bearing his cross went forth into a place called ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of a skull, which is called in the Hebrew, Golgotha:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where they crucified him, and two others with him, on each side one, and Jesus in the midst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pilate wrote a title, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the cross. And the writing was, JESUS OF NAZARETH THE KING OF THE JEWS.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many of the Jews then read this title: for the place where Jesus was crucified was nigh to the city: and it was written in Hebrew, Greek, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Latin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said the chief priests of the Jews to Pilate, Write not, The King of the Jews; but that he said, I am King of the Jews.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pilate answered, What I have written, I have written.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the soldiers, when they had crucified Jesus, took his garments, and made four parts, to every soldier a part; and also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " coat: now the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They said therefore among themselves, Let us not rend it, but cast lots for it whose it shall be: that the scripture might be fulfilled, which saith, They parted my raiment among them, and for my vesture they cast lots. These things therefore the soldiers did.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now there stood by the cross of Jesus, his mother, and his mother's sister, Mary the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wife",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Cleophas, and Mary Magdalene.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Jesus therefore saw his mother, and the disciple standing by, whom he loved, he saith to his mother, Woman, behold thy son!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith he to the disciple, Behold thy mother! And from that hour that disciple took her to his own ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "home",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this, Jesus knowing that all things were now accomplished, that the scripture might be fulfilled, saith, I thirst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now there was set a vessel full of vinegar: and they filled a spunge with vinegar, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon hyssop, and put ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and expired.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Jews therefore, because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath, (for that sabbath was a great day,) besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they might be taken away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came the soldiers, and broke the legs of the first, and of the other who was crucified with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when they came to Jesus, and saw that he was dead already, they broke not his legs:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But one of the soldiers with a spear pierced his side, and forthwith came out blood and water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", testified, and his testimony is true: and he knoweth that he speaketh truth, that ye may believe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For these things were done, that the scripture should be fulfilled, A bone of him shall not be broken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And again another scripture saith, They shall look on him whom they pierced.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And after this, Joseph of Arimathea (being a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jews) besought Pilate that he might take away the body of Jesus: and Pilate gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " leave. He came therefore and took the body of Jesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there came also Nicodemus (who at the first came to Jesus by night) and brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about a hundred pound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "weight",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they took the body of Jesus, and wound it in linen cloths, with the spices, as the manner of the Jews is to bury.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now in the place where he was crucified, there was a garden; and in the garden a new sepulcher, in which was never man yet laid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.19.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.19.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There they laid Jesus therefore, because of the Jews' preparation -",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", for the sepulcher was nigh at hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
